#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
hue — Philips Hue CLI

Turn lights/rooms on/off, set brightness/colour temperature/colour, activate
scenes, list what exists, and pair with the bridge.

API: CLIP v2 (https://<bridge>/clip/v2/resource/...).
Only pair uses v1 POST /api because that is the only way to mint a key.

TLS: The bridge cert is self-signed by Signify. This tool skips verification
(ssl._create_unverified_context). Pinning the Signify root CA is a future
step; the threat model is a home LAN.

Config: ~/.config/hue/config.json ({"bridge": "192.168.1.100", "key": "..."})
mode 0600. Override via --bridge/--key or HUE_BRIDGE/HUE_CONFIG.

Exit codes:
  0  ok
  1  bridge unreachable / HTTP error / timeout
  2  usage (argparse)
  3  target or scene not found / ambiguous
  4  not paired (no config) or key rejected (401)
  5  pair timed out (link button not pressed)
"""

